# Competency question (native gmeow:reasoningLogic lane): "Does the E8 group-action
# law (g·h)·x = g·(h·x), evaluated as a real logic:Formula over a concrete compatible action,
# ENTAIL that both association orders reach the same point?"  The comp(·,·,·)/act(·,·,·) atoms
# are fixed-arity n-ary predications the native reasoner reifies and joins; firing the law
# DERIVES the binary consequent eq(gaWr, gaWr), present in the closure only because the law
# fired. VALUES pins the query to the group-action witness. Over the closure: exactly {gaWr}.
PREFIX exa: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/algebra/>

SELECT ?value WHERE {
    VALUES ?value { exa:gaWr }
    ?value exa:eqRel ?value .
}
